—“a degraded but acceptable U.S. capability” to fulfill our obligations under the
                    Mutual Defense Treaty (MDT) can be maintained only if qualified civilian
                    contractors can be hired to perform certain tasks;

—elimination of all non-MDT related activities on Taiwan, such as aircraft
                    programmed depot maintenance (PDM), adverse effects on PACOM readiness and other
                    military requirements and at considerable unprogrammed expense;
